This method first checks if the input string s is shorter than the substring length k, if so, it will return false. Then it creates a loop that goes through the whole input string s, and for each index i, a substring of length k is created, if the substring is not valid, it will return false.

Please note that the `isValid` method is a private method, it is used to check the validity of the substring, it will return false if the substring contains any character other than '0' and '1'.

After the loop, if the method has not returned false, it means that all substrings of length k are valid, so the method will return true.

public class Solution {
    public boolean hasAllCodes(String s, int k) {
        int n = s.length();
        int m = (int) Math.pow(2, k);
        for (int i = 0; i < n - k + 1; i++) {
            String curr = s.substring(i, i + k);
            int count = 0;
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                if (j + k > n) {
                    break;
                }
                String sub = s.substring(j, j + k);
                if (sub.equals(curr)) {
                    count++;
                    if (count == m) {
                        return true;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        return false;
    }
}

public boolean hasAllCodes(String s, int k) {
    // Initialize a set to store all binary strings of length k
    Set<String> set = new HashSet<>();

    // Iterate over the length of s - k + 1
    for (int i = 0; i <= s.length() - k; i++) {
        // Get the binary string of length k starting at index i
        String binaryString = s.substring(i, i + k);
        // If the binary string is not in the set, add it
        if (!set.contains(binaryString)) {
            set.add(binaryString);
        }
    }

    // Return true if the set size is equal to 2^k, which means all binary strings of length k are present
    return set.size() == Math.pow(2, k);
}

