public static int minPerfectSquareSum(int n) {
    int count = 0;
    while (n > 0) {
        int root = (int) Math.sqrt(n);
        count++;
        n -= root * root;
    }
    return count;
}
```
This method works by repeatedly subtracting the square of the integer part of the square root of n from n until n becomes 0. The number of subtractions needed is returned as the minimum number of perfect square numbers needed to sum up to n.

